# Built artefacts - rebuild with the command in README section 1. The
# pre-2026-09-11 backup binary is also kept out: vendor/BUILD_20260911.md
# records its sha256, which is enough to re-check the identity claim.
vendor/orca.exe
vendor/orca
vendor/*.exe

# Local agent and editor state. Never publish: .obsidian holds a REST-API key,
# and the rest are per-machine session files with absolute paths in them.
.obsidian/
.remember/
.codex/
.claude/
.mcp.json

# Caches. Features/targets/registries are cheap to regenerate; cascades are
# large (~50-75 MB per network) and regenerate in seconds.
cache_cascades_*.npy
cache_oof_*.npz

# Raw corpora are other people's data. fetch_data.py retrieves them and
# records the checksums in data/manifest.json, which IS tracked.
data/*.txt
data/synthetic/

__pycache__/
*.pyc

# The BRAVA/ABCDE external corpus (~3 GB of public, re-downloadable third-party
# data). Stabilised here 2026-09-10 out of a volatile temp scratchpad; identity
# recorded in results/phase6_brava_corpus_identity_20260910.json.
data/brava/

# --- Run outputs too large for git (about 38 GB in total) ----------------------
# Buffered-CV per-cell checkpoints, fold assignments and OOF arrays, both live
# and in the pre-orbit5 retag archive. The summary CSVs and the manifests
# that hash these outputs ARE tracked, so the published numbers still trace back.
results/**/phase6_buffered_cv_checkpoints/
results/**/phase6_buffered_cv_assignments/
results/**/phase6_buffered_cv_oof/
results/**/phase6_buffered_cv_preflight.json
results/**/phase6_buffered_cv_folds.csv

# Superseded pre-refit backups: the OOF arrays from before the orbit5 retag
# and the cache archive. Kept on disk for audit; their hashes are recorded in
# the coverage ledger.
estimators/*.preorbit5
cache_archive/

# Controller and process logs: run traces, not results. One is 107 MB, over
# GitHub's 100 MB per-file limit. Leftover lock files from recovery runs too.
results/**/*.log
results/logs/
results/**/*.lock

# Third-party material collected for checking prior work: published papers
# (PDF plus text extracts) and BRAVA's source code. Not ours to redistribute;
# the provenance JSON beside them records where each one came from.
results/phase6_sources/*.pdf
results/phase6_sources/*.txt
results/phase6_sources/*.py
